Chapter: ZigbeeEncodeTest

  cites Encode chapter Zigbee

 Exercise Zigbee NWK and APS framing: frame-control packing and full
 NWK-data and APS-data frames. Byte sequences checked against the
 Zigbee PRO layout. opening returns the count of passing checks.

Section: Helpers

  bytes-eq : List Integer, List Integer -> Boolean
  bytes-eq (a) (b) =
   if list-length a /= list-length b then False
   else bytes-eq-loop a b 0 (list-length a)

  bytes-eq-loop : List Integer, List Integer, Integer, Integer -> Boolean
  bytes-eq-loop (a) (b) (i) (len) =
   if i >= len then True
   else if list-at a i /= list-at b i then False
   else bytes-eq-loop a b (i + 1) len

  flag : Boolean -> Integer
  flag (b) = if b then 1 else 0

Section: Checks

  check-nwk-fc : Integer
  check-nwk-fc =
   flag (zb-nwk-fc zb-nwk-type-data zb-nwk-version 0 0 == 8)

  check-nwk-frame : Integer
  check-nwk-frame =
   flag (bytes-eq (zb-build-nwk-data #1234 #5678 30 5 [1, 2, 3]) [8, 0, 52, 18, 120, 86, 30, 5, 1, 2, 3])

  check-aps-ack : Integer
  check-aps-ack =
   flag (zb-aps-fc zb-aps-type-data 0 1 0 == 64)

  check-aps-frame : Integer
  check-aps-frame =
   flag (bytes-eq (zb-build-aps-data 1 #0006 #0104 1 10 [1]) [0, 1, 6, 0, 4, 1, 1, 10, 1])

  opening : Integer =
   let a = check-nwk-fc
   in let b = check-nwk-frame
   in let c = check-aps-ack
   in let d = check-aps-frame
   in a + b + c + d
